<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Oultrejordain</h1><p class="st-meta">1118 CE – 1189 CE (approx.) · capital Kerak</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Crusader lordship east of the Jordan, whose castles of Kerak and Montreal controlled the routes between Syria, Egypt and Arabia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Baldwin I built the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shobak-castle">Montreal</a> at Shobak in 1115 to control the land beyond the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">Jordan</a>, and the region was organised as a lordship from around 1118. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/payen-the-butler">Payen the Butler</a> built the great castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-karak">Kerak</a> in 1142, which became its centre.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lordship taxed the caravans and pilgrims moving between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hijaz</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> of the region. It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-milly">Philip of Milly</a> and then, through the heiress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephanie-of-milly">Stephanie of Milly</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raynald-of-chatillon">Raynald of Chatillon</a> in 1176. Raynald raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast in 1182-1183, threatening <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, and attacked a caravan in breach of a truce, provoking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raynald-of-chatillon">Raynald</a> was executed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> after the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> in 1187. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-karak">Kerak</a> surrendered after a long siege in 1188 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shobak-castle">Montreal</a> in 1189; the castles became Ayyubid strongholds.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-oultrejordain.jpg" alt="Lordship of Oultrejordain" width="320" height="410"><figcaption>Image: Erenow · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oultrejordain.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1118 CE – 1189 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kerak</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Payen the Butler, Philip of Milly, Raynald of Châtillon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Transjordan (crusader), Lordship of Montreal</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1154&amp;focus=lordship-of-oultrejordain" aria-label="Lordship of Oultrejordain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5627 1062 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Oultrejordain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5947 1318h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5947 1318h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Jordan. <a href="/atlas?year=1154&amp;focus=lordship-of-oultrejordain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

